Subject: vocabulary q.

   From: D Anton Sherwood <dasher@well.sf.ca.us>

   And while I'm up:
   > 'The Lydians were the first nation to introduce the use of gold and
   > silver coins, and the first who sold goods by retail.'  So says
   > Herodotus . . .

   What does "retail" mean??

retail vs. wholesale

"retail" means to sell in small quantities, to individual consumers,
like what you'd buy in a store

"wholesale" means to sell in large lots, to retailers, like what the
store would buy from its suppliers

The underlying idea in the above passage is that before there was
coined money, people didn't buy their necessities from stores or
markets, they were allocated goods from common warehouses by a
rationing system.

Dale

